e, we get\n\n$$\ny=-2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+b \\\\ 6 & =-2(2)+b \\\\ 6 & =-4+b \\\\ 10 & =b \\\\ b & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-2x+10.\n$$" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247838 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247839 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247840 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247841 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247842 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1041 "selection" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247842 13194139533708 true] [17592186247837 1110 #uuid "c24bdab6-a9a1-505c-8c97-8126c5747911" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247838 1034 "y=-3x+12" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533708 true] [17592186247838 1111 #uuid "ec7b281b-c060-5115-ba7f-5f12a298bed9" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247839 1034 "y=-0.5x+9" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533708 true] [17592186247839 1111 #uuid "30bb6390-7c3b-5f68-b4c4-4d709f90c81a" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247840 1034 "y=-x+12" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533708 true] [17592186247840 1111 #uuid "d7452534-b1e2-5615-9ed3-a9436967e6f6" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247841 1034 "y=-x+10" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247841 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533708 true] [17592186247841 1111 #uuid "1b64ef8d-69a2-5d6b-b9de-a75b9f706368" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247842 1034 "y=-2x+10" 13194139533708 true] [17592186247842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533708 true] [17592186247842 1111 #uuid "509f7578-fc59-56b3-803f-671282d